# Reawakening OS live medium only.
#
# The live desktop account has no password by design (0500-session.hook.chroot
# runs `passwd -d refurb`), so ordinary sudo cannot authenticate at all and the
# user is left with no way to run the installer, enable Cockpit or use the
# diagnostics. The live session is already an unauthenticated physical session:
# tty1 autologins this account without a password. Passwordless sudo therefore
# does not widen access on the medium; it makes the medium usable.
#
# This file is deliberately installed only on the live image. refurb-install
# deletes it from the installed system, whose account has a real password and
# uses the normal %sudo rule. Remote Cockpit access still requires a password
# (set with `refurb-cockpit password`) and stays off until `refurb-cockpit on`.
refurb ALL=(ALL:ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL
